      },
      {
       "evidenceCode": "ECO:0000269",
       "source": "PubMed",
       "id": "28848044"
      }
     ],
     "value": "Nucleotide exchange factor (NEF) for mitochondrial HSP70 (mt-HSP70/HSPA9), facilitating the release of ADP from HSPA9 to allow ATP rebinding, which is essential for the chaperone cycle (PubMed:28848044). Functions as a component of the presequence translocase-associated motor (PAM) complex, which drives ATP-dependent import of proteins into the mitochondrial matrix. In the PAM complex, supports the HSPA9-driven pulling mechanism that translocates polypeptides through the TIM23 complex (PubMed:28848044). May control the nucleotide-dependent binding of HSPA9 to substrate proteins (PubMed:11311562)"
    }
   ],
   "commentType": "FUNCTION"
  },
  {
   "texts": [
    {
     "evidences": [
      {
       "evidenceCode": "ECO:0000250",
       "source": "UniProtKB",
       "id": "P38523"
      },
      {
       "evidenceCode": "ECO:0000269",
       "source": "PubMed",
       "id": "11311562"
      },
      {
       "evidenceCode": "ECO:0000269",
       "source": "PubMed",
       "id": "30098457"
      },
      {
       "evidenceCode": "ECO:0000269",
       "source": "PubMed",
       "id": "39737924"
      }
     ],
     "value": "Homodimer (PubMed:30098457, PubMed:39737924). Component of the PAM complex at least composed of mitochondrial HSP70/HSPA9, GRPEL1 or GRPEL2, TIMM44, TIMM16/PAM16 and TIMM14/DNAJC19 (By similarity). Binds HSP70 (mitochondrial/HSPA9 and cytosolic), HSC70 and HSJ1B (PubMed:11311562, PubMed:30098457)"
    }
   ],
